President Trump announced new efforts to  get crucial supplies like masks gloves  and surgical gowns to medical centers  amid shortages in this country the US  Surgeon General dr. Jerome Adams joins  us from Washington he's a member of the  White House Coronas virus task force dr.  Adams thank you so much for joining us I  know you're hearing a - we are hearing  heartbreaking stories from doctors who  say they cannot get the basics for the  first time we're hearing doctors say I'm  scared I'm scared of leaving my children  without a parent because I could  possibly die doing the job that I love  to do what can you say to these people  today it's no longer good enough to say  we're working on it it's coming help us  on the way you have to help us  understand why this is so difficult and  what you guys are doing right now to  remedy this situation well good morning  and I didn't expect to be starting off  my week with such a dire message for  America but the numbers are going to get  worse this week things are going to get  worse before they get better  and we really need everyone to  understand this is serious to lean into  what they can do to to flatten the curve  and you talked about health care workers  I'm getting those calls every minute of  the day I got calls from people  literally while I was sitting here  waiting to talk to you and I want the  health care workers of America to  understand these are my colleagues these  are my friends and I will not rest until  you all have the tools you need to keep  ourselves we know everything you've just  said we've all heard this a gazillion  times why is this so difficult and I'm  not going to be disrespectful  no no frustrated not at all and I'll  tell you why it's difficult because the  national stockpile purchases 1/10 of 1%  of all the medical supplies in this  country the rest of it is in the market  and so we're doing a couple of things  and I want people to know the tangible  actions were taking we are using the  stockpile through FEMA which has been  activated to level 1 to send out  supplies than they are we sent out over  2 million  masks there are supplies going out to  the places most at need Washington  California New York we have the military  out on the ground in several of these  places we found out CDC teams to provide  backup we've worked with the American  Society of anise  geologists to identify 70,000  ventilators that are in the O R that can  be converted so supplies are going out  we know that they're not going out fast  enough to keep pace with the demand and  that's why the most important message I  have for America is we are halfway  through our 15 days to stop the spread  we need to turn the spigot off  we can't ventilate we can't ventilate  our way out of this problem we need to  make sure in addition to getting  supplies to people that we're really  focusing on demand and getting people  out of the streets stay at home but dr.  Adams the President signed the defense  production Act he can essentially order  companies to manufacture these supplies  that medical professionals professionals  so desperately need at this point why  isn't the government doing that the  government is using the defense  production act to get people to the  table we've worked with 3m we've worked  with Honeywell they are already at max  production here's the thing people don't  understand you don't need to compel  someone to do something that they are  already doing and so yo every single day  there are people looking and saying do  we need to compel someone to do this  let's make the call okay they're already  at max production they're already  working around the clock and again we  are using the stockpile and FEMA to get  resources out to people who need it  we're finding new and innovative people  who were stepping up and volunteering  like Hanes would have never thought that  Hanes would be able to produce surgical  masks they're producing masks we're  hearing reports of shortages on personal  protective equipment and you're saying  we're already at mass max production  does that mean shortages are just gonna  be the way it is well we know that there  are going to be shortages in some areas  and it's why I actually wrote an op-ed  calling on people to stop elective  surgeries we need to make sure that  supplies are getting to New York to  California to Washington to the places  they need and they can't get there if  people are out somewhere else where they  don't see cases right now doing elective  procedures we want to make sure we're  strategically moving the the personal  protective equipment and supplies to  where it is most needed and that's both  supply and driving down demand dr. I'd  like to ask you about things getting  worse and when we might be able to pull  back on some of these restrictions on  movement the president tweeted recently  we cannot let the Cure be worse than the  problem itself and I think a lot of  people would agree that this economic  shutdown is very painful for people but  a medical perspective realistically is  there any chance at the end of this  15-day period we're just gonna go back  to anything like normal well we know  it's gonna be a while before life gets  back to normal and here's what what I  want America to know we don't want to  wait for 15 days we don't want to wait  another day I'm looking at them driving  in and seeing people out all over the  place getting ready for cherry blossoms  on you you you you look on the news and  you see people still at beaches we don't  have a day to waste and what we need to  do is focus on today this our doctor  right now  doctor how far away from the peak of  this do you think we are because some  people have said it's it's not before  the end of April well when you look at  the China data they were able to hit  their peak and come back down at about  six to eight weeks when you look at the  Italy data they're still going up so we  are somewhere between the two and it's  gonna be up to everyone coming together  to drive down demand to determine  whether our curve bends in the direction  of China in six to eight weeks or  whether it bends towards Italy and  unfortunately we're seeing that New York  it's approaching Italy why because the  numbers that you see if cases reflect  what happened two weeks ago and too many  people are waiting too long to really  take these 15 days to stop the spread  initiative seriously didn't have a 15  days to stop the spread voluntary  restrictions they were much more  draconian than that are you saying we  need more stringent recommendations well  in the United States we have a system of  federalism and the governors are in  charge of determining what's appropriate  to their states here's what I'm saying  and we work we've worked well with with  many of the governors with most of the  governors we need everyone if you  weren't seeing cases right now now's the  time you need to be making sure you're  doing the things so that you don't  become the next New York or the next  Italy all right dr. Jerome Adams thank  you so much for being with us this  morning  and if you're healthy you can still  still get blood all right thanks dr.  Adams
 

